\f0  Army Card Prototype \'96 Gameplay & Systems Overview\
\
## Core Concept\
A **turn-based auto-battler with deck-building elements**.\
\
Players build an army over multiple rounds by **drawing cards, buying units with gold, arranging formations**, and then watching **deterministic combat resolve automatically**.\
\
There is no manual control during combat \'97 all strategy happens **before** combat begins.\
\
---\
\
## 
\f1 \uc0\u55358 \u56813 
\f0  Battle Flow\
\
Each battle consists of multiple rounds (currently **3**), unless ended early by commander death.\
\
### Round Structure\
\
1. **Gold Phase**\
   - Round 1: players gain a larger starting gold amount\
   - Rounds 2+: players gain a fixed gold per round\
\
2. **Draw Phase**\
   - Round 1: players draw a starting hand (e.g. 10 cards)\
   - Rounds 2+: players draw +1 card at the start of the round\
\
3. **Buy Phase**\
   - Players spend gold to play unit cards from hand onto the battlefield\
   - Units are placed automatically by heuristics (temporary)\
   - Purchased cards are discarded after use\
 -Players alternate buy phase, player A buys then B then A and so on until can\'92t buy or pass\
4. Buy phase abilities\
	- some units/unit cards have abilities that trigger immediately after being bought which is equivalent to being placed on the field. \
\
5. **Rearrangement Phase** *(rounds \uc0\u8805  2)*\
   - Units may be reordered within rows\
   - Front and Middle rows may be swapped\
   - Back row remains fixed\
   - Current logic uses simple heuristics (e.g. higher HP units move forward)\
\
6. **Combat Phase**\
