\
## 
\f1 \uc0\u55358 \u56817 
\f0  Battlefield Model\
\
Each player has **three rows**:\
\
- **Front**\
- **Middle**\
- **Back**\
\
### Targeting Rules\
- Damage is applied **Front 
\f2 \uc0\u8594 
\f0  Middle 
\f2 \uc0\u8594 
\f0  Back**\
- Commander is protected unless:\
  - All units are destroyed\
  - Leftover damage remains\
\
---\
\
## 
\f1 \uc0\u55358 \u56982 
\f0  Units\
\
Each unit has:\
-Name\
- HP\
- ATK\
- Cost\
- Type\
-Pre-emptive strike\
-ability\
-ability data\
\
\
### Unit Types\
- **Infantry** \'96 typically Front\
- **Vehicle / Ranged** \'96 typically Middle\
- **Air** \'96 typically Back\
\
Some units may have **special effects** (e.g. pre-emptive strikes or ask multipliers).\
\
---\
\
## 
\f1 \uc0\u9876 \u65039 
\f0  Combat Resolution\
\
Combat is deterministic and resolves in phases.\
\
### 1. Pre-emptive Phase\
- Certain units may perform **pre-emptive strikes**\
- All pre-emptive damage resolves simultaneously\
- Units destroyed here do **not** contribute to main attack\
\
### 2. Main Combat Phase\
- Each side\'92s **total ATK** is calculated from all surviving units\
- Damage is applied row-by-row\
- Damage spills from unit to unit\
- Every damage allocation is logged as an event\
- abilities may trigger\
\
### 3. Cleanup Phase\
- Dead units are removed from rows\
- Dead units are moved to discard piles\
\
---\
\
## 
\f1 \uc0\u55357 \u56540 
\f0  Event System\
\
Combat generates a **CombatReport**, containing an ordered list of `CombatEvent`s.\
\
### Event Types Include\
- `CombatStart`\
- `CombatEnd`\
- `PreemptiveStrikeDeclared`\
- `DamageAppliedToUnit`\
- `UnitDestroyed`\
- `CommanderDamaged`\
- `CleanupMovedToDiscard`\
- Debug / summary events (row start/end, damage summaries)\
\
### Playback\
- `CombatPlayback` replays events using a coroutine\
- Events are processed sequentially with optional delays\
- Designed to later support:\
  - Animations\
  - VFX\
  - UI hooks\
  - Replay / speed control\
\
---\
\
## 
\f1 \uc0\u55356 \u56527 
\f0  Deck & Economy System\
\
### Deck\
- Players start with a predefined deck\
- Deck is shuffled once at battle start\
- Cards are drawn into hand\
- Played cards are discarded\
\
### Gold\
- Gold persists between rounds\
- Gold is spent only during Buy Phase\
- No selling or refunds yet\
\
---\
\
## 
\f1 \uc0\u9989 
\f0  Current Features\
\
- Full multi-round battle loop\
- Draw / Buy / Rearrangement / Combat phases\
- Deterministic combat resolution\
- Pre-emptive strike system\
- Accurate damage allocation with full logging\
- Coroutine-based combat playback\
- Debug-friendly, inspectable event stream\
\
---\
\
## 
\f1 \uc0\u55357 \u56999 
\f0  Planned Features\
\
### Short-Term\
- Manual unit placement (UI-driven)\
- Player-controlled rearrangement\
- Visual battlefield representation\
- Combat animations tied to events\
\
### Medium-Term\
- Unit abilities & triggered effects\
- Buffs & debuffs\
- Status effects (stun, shield, poison)\
- Commander abilities\
\
### Long-Term\
- Persistent deck progression\
- Drafting / shop rerolls\
- PvE encounters and AI scaling\
- PvP simulations\
- Save/load battle states\
- Replay viewer\
\
---\
\
## 
\f1 \uc0\u55356 \u57263 
\f0  Design Philosophy\
\
- **Deterministic & inspectable combat**\
- **Event-driven simulation**\
- **Separation of simulation and presentation**\
- Built for **rapid iteration and testing**\
\
---\
\
## 
\f1 \uc0\u55357 \u57056 \u65039 
\f0  Notes for Developers\
\
- Combat logic lives in `CombatResolver`\
- Playback logic lives in `CombatPlayback`\
- Combat state is communicated exclusively through `CombatEvent`s\
- Logging verbosity is intentional during proof-of-concept stage\
